b5.connexion:
🔗 Your connection
   • Technical name: {f} ({nm})
   • Type: {k}
   • Your computer's address: {ip}
      Why: this is its house number on your network; it lets other devices find it.
   • Box (gateway): {gw}
      Why: it is the way out to the Internet. Everything going out or coming in passes through it.
   • Site directory (DNS): {dns}
      Why: it turns a name like debian.org into a numeric address, like a phone book.
   • Link speed: {spt}
      Why: this is the maximum speed of the cable or Wi-Fi between your computer and the box (it is not the speed of your internet subscription).

